{"availability":"available","full":"VanshGehlot/AGI","name":"AGI","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":null,"stars":51,"forks":9,"created":"2023-07-07T10:38:45Z","updated":"2024-07-18T17:00:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://palm-e.github.io/#demo","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.402Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.402Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.402Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.402Z","stars":51,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Generative artificial intelligence is a branch of AI focused on using machine learning algorithms to generate new content such as images, video, text, and audio. The goal is for AI systems to create unique, original artefacts that seem as if they were created by humans.","The goal of generative AI is to give machines a degree of creative ability and push the boundaries of what AI can accomplish. But it also introduces risks around the plausible spread of misinformation that we must consider seriously. Overall, generative AI is an exciting and fast-moving field of research."],"features":["Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs)(GAN-Zoo): GANs use two neural networks, a generator and a discriminator, that compete against each other to create new data samples. GANs have been used to generate photorealistic…","Variational Autoencoders (VAEs): VAEs are neural networks used for unsupervised learning of compressed latent representations of data. They have been used to generate new data samples such as images, handwriting, and…","Text Generation: Models like GPT-3 can generate paragraphs of coherent text, poetry, articles, and scripts after being trained on massive datasets.","Deepfakes (Link): Deep learning techniques can manipulate or generate visual and audio content with a high potential for misuse. Models can generate fake images, videos, and speech that seem authentic.","Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF)(Link): Algorithms like DeepMind's AlphaGo have gotten smarter at playing complex games by competing against themselves to develop advanced strategies."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VanshGehlot/AGI/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6d220711292db15ed6de909a07ef83e1cfe1fc80e2d83ac09cf36871bd80ba16","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.511Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.511Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Generative artificial intelligence is a branch of AI focused on using machine learning algorithms to generate new content such as images, video, text, and audio. The goal is for AI systems to create unique, original artefacts that seem as if they were created by humans.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VanshGehlot/AGI/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6d220711292db15ed6de909a07ef83e1cfe1fc80e2d83ac09cf36871bd80ba16","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VanshGehlot/AGI/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.511Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-07-18T17:00:40Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VanshGehlot/AGI/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:38.512Z","hash":"6d220711292db15ed6de909a07ef83e1cfe1fc80e2d83ac09cf36871bd80ba16","originalBytes":13623,"storedBytes":13623,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["language","website","models","learning","paper","generate","generative","google","they","arxiv","code","llms","data","engineering","large","networks","neural","prompt","robotics","text","harvard","images","like","llm","model","stanford","artificial","gans","genai","include","intelligence","introduction","microsoft","resources","some","transformer","transformers","used","advanced","algorithms","basics","been","content","data.","educational","everyone","general","gpt-4","human","intro","link","machine","multimodal","new","pro","reasoning","robots","se